// Tessera stdlib: tables shared by the correctly rounded F16 sinh, cosh and tanh
//
// The tables hold F32 bit patterns. An F16 input x with bits u splits as
// x = x1 + x2, where x1 has bits (u >> 5) << 5 (index i1 = u >> 5) and x2 keeps
// the sign, exponent and low 5 mantissa bits (index i2 = ((u >> 10) << 5) |
// (u & 0x1f)).
//
// Ported from CORE-MATH, src/binary16/sinh/sinhf16.c (also used verbatim by
// src/binary16/tanh/tanhf16.c and, for C2, src/binary16/cosh/coshf16.c) via
// RazorForge's B16HypTables.rf.
// Copyright (c) 2025 Paul Zimmermann
// MIT license: see LICENSE-CORE-MATH

module Standard::Core

